<template>
    <heading>Model</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>model</li>
        <li>project</li>
        <li>directory handle</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p><code>window.LP5.model</code> holds the application's project state. <code>model.directoryHandle</code> starts as <code>null</code>; <code>model.setDirectoryHandle(handle)</code> installs a selected directory handle, or clears it with <code>null</code>.</p>
        <p>The model holds state in memory. Permission requests, project loading, and IndexedDB persistence are separate operations. Once loading is implemented, the handle and loaded articles should be installed together after a successful load.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>model</name>
        <code><![CDATA[let model = (() => {
    let directoryHandle = null;

    function setDirectoryHandle(handle) {
        directoryHandle = handle;
    }

    return {
        get directoryHandle() { return directoryHandle; },
        setDirectoryHandle
    };
})();
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
